WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.208 --> 00:00:14.768
Zann yelled.

2
00:00:14.788 --> 00:00:17.770
"We'll meet you on the other side of the boulder.

3
00:00:18.111 --> 00:00:19.592
Then we can all zap away!"

4
00:00:20.472 --> 00:00:22.414
Darb nodded and darted out of sight.

5
00:00:23.154 --> 00:00:24.755
The blue dragons waddled after him.

6
00:00:25.676 --> 00:00:29.178
Zann and the others ran in the opposite direction, with Perda in the lead.

7
00:00:30.019 --> 00:00:32.981
Suddenly she stopped, and Zann almost crashed into her.

8
00:00:34.202 --> 00:00:35.283
He quickly saw why.

9
00:00:36.043 --> 00:00:38.805
Arrano was nearby, talking to several adults.

10
00:00:38.825 --> 00:00:41.587
"Arrano!" Zann exclaimed.

11
00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:43.268
"Where did you go before?"

12
00:00:44.049 --> 00:00:45.269
Arrano turned to face him.

13
00:00:45.289 --> 00:00:48.672
"I had to summon the others before you got yourselves in trouble."

14
00:00:49.452 --> 00:00:54.015
Just then Darb and Zing came around the other side of the boulder, running fast.

15
00:00:54.035 --> 00:00:56.077
"They're right behind me!"

16
00:00:56.357 --> 00:00:56.937
Darb cried.

17
00:00:56.957 --> 00:00:58.859
"Oh dear."

18
00:00:59.299 --> 00:01:00.580
One of the adults bit her lip.

19
00:01:01.108 --> 00:01:02.529
"You must have angered them."

20
00:01:02.549 --> 00:01:07.151
"Quick! Get behind us," a man said as Darb reached the group.

21
00:01:08.092 --> 00:01:14.095
Zann grabbed Zing and huddled with his friends behind the Dracians, expecting them to fend off the dragons.

22
00:01:14.896 --> 00:01:19.938
But instead of fighting, the Dracians threw themselves onto their knees in front of the small creatures.

23
00:01:19.958 --> 00:01:22.300
"What are they doing?"

24
00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:23.300
Gliss whispered.

25
00:01:24.081 --> 00:01:24.781
Zann shrugged.

26
00:01:25.902 --> 00:01:29.624
The Dracians were talking now, but Zann couldn't understand their words.

27
00:01:30.644 --> 00:01:32.065
"Weird," Perda murmured.

28
00:01:32.085 --> 00:01:35.248
"It sounds like they're begging or something."

29
00:01:36.169 --> 00:01:36.929
Darb nodded.

30
00:01:36.949 --> 00:01:39.972
"And they must be speaking in the dragons' language."

31
00:01:41.473 --> 00:01:44.115
The dragons looked irritated as they listened to the humans.

32
00:01:45.096 --> 00:01:48.338
One dragon spit a small glob of lava near the Dracians.

33
00:01:49.279 --> 00:01:52.421
Finally both dragons turned and waddled away.

34
00:01:53.462 --> 00:01:54.883
The Dracians climbed to their feet.

35
00:01:56.024 --> 00:01:57.546
Arrano hurried over to Zann.

36
00:01:58.086 --> 00:02:00.268
"Let's go before the dragons change their minds."

37
00:02:01.152 --> 00:02:04.674
The Dracians rushed away, and Zann and his friends followed.

38
00:02:05.595 --> 00:02:09.057
Finally everyone stopped in the shelter of a rock overhang.

39
00:02:09.077 --> 00:02:12.018
"Whew!" one of the adults said.

40
00:02:12.038 --> 00:02:19.182
"You kids are lucky the first dragons you encountered were lava leapers instead of something bigger and less

41
00:02:19.262 --> 00:02:21.704
reasonable." Arrano nodded.

42
00:02:21.724 --> 00:02:25.726
"Most dragons would have roasted you just for looking directly at them."

43
00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.387
"What are you talking about?"

44
00:02:28.608 --> 00:02:29.128
Zann said.

45
00:02:29.696 --> 00:02:32.757
"Dragons don't usually attack people without a good reason."

46
00:02:34.098 --> 00:02:34.878
Darb shrugged.

47
00:02:35.378 --> 00:02:36.919
"Maybe things are different here."

48
00:02:37.819 --> 00:02:39.340
One of the adults eyed Zing.

49
00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.621
"Why does this dragon travel with you?"

50
00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:42.261
he asked.

51
00:02:42.281 --> 00:02:44.162
"Is he training you?"

52
00:02:44.182 --> 00:02:46.823
"Zing? Training us?"

53
00:02:47.323 --> 00:02:48.023
Perda chuckled.

54
00:02:48.043 --> 00:02:49.864
"He's Zann's pet."

55
00:02:49.884 --> 00:02:54.106
"Pet?" Arrano said the word as if he'd never heard it before.

56
00:02:54.126 --> 00:02:55.667
"What's a pet?"

57
00:02:56.907 --> 00:02:58.008
Zann was confused.

58
00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:03.684
"Uh, he lives in my house and I feed him and play with him and stuff."

59
00:03:05.065 --> 00:03:07.166
"Oh." Arrano's expression cleared.

60
00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:09.108
"You mean you're his servant."

61
00:03:10.009 --> 00:03:13.632
Zann laughed, but quickly realized Arrano wasn't joking.

62
00:03:13.652 --> 00:03:15.613
"Wait," Darb said.

63
00:03:15.633 --> 00:03:17.395
"I get it.

64
00:03:17.815 --> 00:03:20.978
In this world the dragons are the dominant species, aren't they?"

65
00:03:20.998 --> 00:03:22.779
"Of course."

66
00:03:23.259 --> 00:03:24.781
Arrano sounded surprised.

67
00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:26.582
"Isn't it that way everywhere?"

68
00:03:26.602 --> 00:03:28.764
"No," Perda said.

69
00:03:29.324 --> 00:03:31.446
"In Magica, humans are in charge."

70
00:03:32.566 --> 00:03:34.168
The Dracians looked skeptical.

71
00:03:34.188 --> 00:03:36.890
"Humans rule over dragons?"

72
00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:37.890
a woman said.

73
00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:41.293
"Impossible. Who would serve the dragons?"

74
00:03:42.393 --> 00:03:43.414
Another adult nodded.

75
00:03:43.434 --> 00:03:46.036
"And what would the dragons eat?"

76
00:03:47.477 --> 00:03:48.158
Zann gulped.

77
00:03:48.178 --> 00:03:50.960
"Do dragons eat people here?"

78
00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:56.944
"Yes, when necessary," Arrano said, "though most prefer other fare."

79
00:03:57.888 --> 00:03:59.389
Zann wasn't sure what to say.

80
00:04:00.429 --> 00:04:06.472
It was weird to think about living in a world where people were dragons' servants—and sometimes their dinner.

81
00:04:07.372 --> 00:04:08.672
But he pushed the thought aside.

82
00:04:08.693 --> 00:04:11.354
"We're looking for someone," he said.

83
00:04:11.374 --> 00:04:12.854
"Two people, actually.

84
00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:15.755
Their names are Wyssa and Morb."

85
00:04:16.936 --> 00:04:18.637
The Dracians exchanged a glance.

86
00:04:18.657 --> 00:04:21.558
"They were both here," a man said.

87
00:04:21.578 --> 00:04:24.299
"Wyssa left shortly before you kids arrived."

88
00:04:25.299 --> 00:04:26.900
"Yes," another man said.

89
00:04:27.548 --> 00:04:31.310
"She only stayed long enough to determine that Morb had moved on."

90
00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:33.651
"When did Morb leave?"

91
00:04:33.951 --> 00:04:34.591
Perda asked.

92
00:04:34.611 --> 00:04:37.632
"About ten days ago," Arrano said.

93
00:04:37.652 --> 00:04:41.494
"He was here for almost a week, though nobody knew his purpose."

94
00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:45.275
"Did either of them mention World X?"

95
00:04:45.716 --> 00:04:46.316
Zann asked.

96
00:04:46.336 --> 00:04:48.197
"World X?"

97
00:04:48.597 --> 00:04:49.397
A woman shrugged.

98
00:04:49.417 --> 00:04:50.898
"I don't think so.

99
00:04:50.978 --> 00:04:52.659
I've never heard of such a place."

100
00:04:53.799 --> 00:04:55.920
Arrano and the others murmured in agreement.

101
00:04:56.776 --> 00:05:02.678
One of the women cast a nervous glance upward as several large dragons flapped past high overhead.

102
00:05:02.698 --> 00:05:06.299
"You'd better return to the wormhole," she said.

103
00:05:06.319 --> 00:05:08.819
"It won't be long before you're noticed."

104
00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.240
"Good idea."

105
00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:12.100
Zann glanced at his friends.

106
00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.721
"Come on, guys.

107
00:05:14.001 --> 00:05:15.841
Let's zap back to the boiling lake."

108
00:05:16.802 --> 00:05:18.582
"Wait!" Arrano looked alarmed.

109
00:05:19.042 --> 00:05:20.303
"You shouldn't use magic.

110
00:05:20.763 --> 00:05:22.543
Some of the dragons can sense it.

111
00:05:23.303 --> 00:05:25.444
They might get curious and come to investigate."

112
00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.041
All the Dracians were still watching the skies.

113
00:05:29.901 --> 00:05:33.563
Their anxious expressions reminded Zann of the people of Skellia.

114
00:05:34.503 --> 00:05:37.845
He wished he could have helped the Skellians escape their watery world.

115
00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:40.846
Maybe he could help these people now.

116
00:05:41.947 --> 00:05:43.527
"Why don't you guys all come with us?"

117
00:05:43.907 --> 00:05:44.548
he blurted out.

118
00:05:44.568 --> 00:05:50.190
"We could take you to another world where you won't be ruled over by dangerous dragons."

119
00:05:51.631 --> 00:05:54.572
To Zann's surprise the Dracians shook their heads.

120
00:05:55.736 --> 00:05:56.897
"Leave Drac?"

121
00:05:57.217 --> 00:05:57.798
a woman said.

122
00:05:57.818 --> 00:05:59.319
"Oh, we couldn't."

123
00:06:00.559 --> 00:06:02.181
"Thank you," Arrano added.

124
00:06:02.201 --> 00:06:04.242
"But Drac is our home.

125
00:06:04.662 --> 00:06:06.243
We wouldn't want to live anywhere else."

126
00:06:07.384 --> 00:06:10.746
The Dracians offered to guide the visitors on foot to the wormhole.

127
00:06:11.507 --> 00:06:13.388
But Zann could tell that they were afraid.

128
00:06:13.808 --> 00:06:14.489
And no wonder!

129
00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:20.093
He couldn't imagine how it would feel to know that any passing dragon might eat you.

130
00:06:20.113 --> 00:06:24.776
"Thanks, but we remember how to get back to the lake," Zann said.

131
00:06:25.376 --> 00:06:26.056
"Come on, guys."

132
00:06:27.177 --> 00:06:31.638
Zann and his friends said good-bye and then set off through the scorched landscape.

133
00:06:31.658 --> 00:06:35.859
"Are you sure we can't zap to the wormhole?"

134
00:06:36.159 --> 00:06:38.940
Perda complained after a few minutes, mopping her brow.

135
00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:41.841
"We'd better not," Darb said.

136
00:06:41.861 --> 00:06:43.801
"You heard what the Dracians said."

137
00:06:44.662 --> 00:06:46.702
The group walked without talking for a while.

138
00:06:47.602 --> 00:06:49.583
Zann frowned when they crested a ridge.

139
00:06:50.623 --> 00:06:52.524
A patch of tall trees lay below.

140
00:06:53.656 --> 00:06:57.180
"I don't remember seeing any trees like that before."

141
00:06:58.221 --> 00:07:01.085
Zann's heart sank as he realized what this meant.

142
00:07:01.105 --> 00:07:02.927
"We're lost!"
